# expect: cannot be checked against that set
#
# `aria-current` admits five words and a browser maps every other one onto
# `true` rather than ignoring it, so a value that exists only at run time
# would announce a kind of current the program never wrote. There is no
# run-time check that could stand in: the set is the whole rule. What a
# program writes instead is `if`, and `widgets/breadcrumbs.zd` does.
state kind is client Text starting "page"

view
    Column
        Text "Issues", current is kind
